DynaDocs (dydo) - Durable project knowledge and native skills for AI coding assistants.

Setup Commands:
  init <integration>     Initialize DynaDocs (claude, codex, all, none)
  init <int> --join      Join existing project as new team member
  adopt <version>        Record the dydo release the project adopted (dydoVersion)

Documentation Commands:
  check [path]           Validate docs, report violations
  check --root <dir>     Check another project (graph, validate also take --root)
  fix [path]             Auto-fix issues where possible
  index [path]           Regenerate index.md from structure
  graph <file>           Show graph connections for a file
  graph stats [--top N]  Show top docs by incoming links

Linear Commands:
  map [--no-browser]     Serve a read-only map of a Linear Project on localhost
  survey <project>       Print a read-only digest of a Linear Project's lanes

Workspace Commands:
  guard                  Check if action is allowed (for hooks)
  mode show              List this machine's mode flags (overnight)
  mode set <flag> <val>  Set a mode flag, e.g. mode set overnight on
  clean [<worktree>...]  Remove linked worktrees; archives uncommitted work, keeps unmerged branches
  clean --all            Every linked worktree (--dry-run first; --archive lists the archive)
  pr-ready [path]        Check a PR can be opened: clean tree, HEAD pushed (--body checks the body)
  merge <pr> --match-head-commit <sha> --match-base-commit <sha>
                         Merge a reviewed PR into its feature/* branch (--dry-run checks only)

Validation Commands:
  validate               Validate local configuration and nudges
  gap-check [args]       Run the configured coverage gap check
  statechart             Check a TLA+ model or save its prerequisite installation plan
  statechart resume      Install locked prerequisites and continue a saved request
  statechart doctor      Inspect installed statechart assets and local prerequisites offline
  statechart install-skill Install matching statechart skill into an explicit project

Utility:
  completions <shell>    Generate shell completions (bash, zsh, powershell)
  version                Display version information
  help                   Display this help

Exit codes:
  0 - Success / Action allowed
  1 - Validation errors found
  2 - Tool error / Action blocked

For detailed command reference, see: ./dydo/reference/dydo-commands.md

